  <static seed="1237" source="Contrib/PCC/BasicAlgebra/LinearEquationApplications/MXPlusBWordProblem30.pg">
    <statement><p>A school purchased a batch of T-shirts from a company. The company charged <m>{\$10}</m> per T-shirt, and gave the school a <m>{\$50}</m> rebate. If the school had a net expense of <m>{\$3{,}850}</m> from the purchase, how many T-shirts did the school buy?</p>
<p>The school purchased <fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0001"/> T-shirts.</p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>390</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><p>Let <m>x</m> be the number of T-shirts the school purchased.</p>
<p>Each T-shirt costs <m>{\$10}</m>, so <m>x</m> T-shirts cost <m>10x</m> dollars. After that expense, there was a rebate of 50 dollars.</p>
<p>Now we can write an equation:</p>
<p><m>\displaystyle{ 10x-50 = 3850 }</m></p>
<p>Next, we solve for <m>x</m>:</p>
<p><m>\begin{aligned}
  10x -50 \amp = 3850 \\
  10x -50\mathbf{{}+50} \amp = 3850\mathbf{{}+50} \\
  10x      \amp = 3900 \\
  \frac{10x}{10} \amp = \frac{3900}{10} \\
  x   \amp = 390
\end{aligned}</m></p>
<p>The school purchased <m>390</m> T-shirts.</p>
</solution>
